    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2286" root="برص" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرْصٌ</span></b>  <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَزَغَةٌ</span> [<i>A lizard of the species called
gecko, of a leprous hue,</i> as its name <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">برص</span> indicates;
so applied in the present day]; (TA;) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبُو</span>
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرِيصٍ</span></b> , (M,) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبُو بُرَيْصٍ</span></b> , (TA,) is <i>a surname
of the same.</i> (M, TA.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرْصٌ</span>; and see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَامُّ أَبْرَصَ</span>, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبْرَصُ</span>; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرِيصَةً</span>.]

